Article 7 (Site Selection Division)
(1) The Head of the Site Selection Division shall be a public official of Grade IV.
(2) The Head of the Site Selection Division shall be responsible for the following matters:
1. Establishment and implementation of survey plans for the suitability of sites for high-level radioactive waste management facilities (hereinafter referred to as "management facilities");
2. Preparation and coordination of procedures, methods, and evaluation criteria for selecting sites for management facilities;
3. Implementation of preliminary and in-depth surveys of site suitability for management facilities;
4. Selection of and cancellation of the selection of sites for management facilities;
5. Composition and operation of the Support Committee for Areas Hosting Management Facilities;
6. Establishment and implementation of support plans for areas hosting management facilities;
7. Matters concerning the provision of special support grants under Article 28 of the Act;
8. Approval of standards for the operation of management facilities;
9. Approval of facility plans for spent nuclear fuel storage facilities within nuclear power plant sites (hereinafter referred to as "on-site storage facilities");
10. Support for areas surrounding on-site storage facilities.
